    Behavior notes
    - 'Total' is the whole-order total; per-unit price = Total / quantity when qty > 1, rounded to 2dp (e.g. 58.00/2 -> 29.00, 9.99/3 -> 3.33). This keeps the analytics invariant price * quantity == order Total — asserted explicitly in the tests.
    - Refunded iff Financial status contains 'refund' (covers 'refunded' and 'partially refunded'); 'voided' and 'paid' are not refunded. Negative total also marks refunded, mirroring core.
    - Shopify's '-0400' offset dates parse via datetime.fromisoformat and are stripped to naive datetimes (2026-06-01 14:32:00 -0400 -> datetime(2026,6,1,14,32)).
    - 'Total' outranks 'Subtotal' in the synonym priority so a full Shopify export never prices by line-item subtotal; extra columns (Shipping, Tags, etc.) are ignored.
    - Never raises: bad date / bad price / missing product / ragged rows warn + skip; bad quantity defaults to 1; empty CSV and missing required columns return warnings.
    
